Spec: MCP server adapter

Purpose:
  The Model Context Protocol interface to the application: a single Streamable HTTP endpoint at `/mcp` where AI
  agents list and read every entity anonymously, and create, edit and delete entities when they present the
  shared bearer token. A driving adapter over the other feature packages' services.py, following
  ../architecture.sdd, with no entity, persistence or view of its own.

Structure:
  ./services.py: SDK-free adaptation layer: the write-token guard, entity-to-dict serializers, ISO 8601 input
    parsing and the conversion of each feature's validation and lookup errors into the package-local @McpError
  ./server.py: the driving adapter; builds the `mcp` SDK's @MCPServer, one tool per operation, per
    ../architecture.sdd

Owns:
  ./__init__.py
  ./services.py
  ./server.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Depends on:
  ../shared/shared.sdd
  ../courses/courses.sdd
  ../semester/semester.sdd
  ../realizations/realizations.sdd
  ../lessons/lessons.sdd
  ../holidays/holidays.sdd
  ../no_teach_weeks/no_teach_weeks.sdd
  ../week_themes/week_themes.sdd
  ../deadlines/deadlines.sdd

Exposes:
  @create_mcp_server in ./server.py, building the MCP server from @McpService and @McpWriteGuard for
    ../main.py to mount.
  Anonymous read tools: `list_semesters`, `list_courses`, `get_course`, `get_realization`, `list_realizations`,
    `get_lesson`, `list_lessons`, `list_lessons_for_range`, `list_holidays`, `list_no_teach_weeks`,
    `get_week_theme`, `list_week_themes`, `get_deadline`, `list_deadlines`, `list_deadlines_for_range`.
  Token-gated write tools: `create_semester`, `delete_semester`, `create_course`, `update_course`,
    `delete_course`, `create_realization`, `update_realization`, `delete_realization`, `create_lesson`,
    `update_lesson`, `delete_lesson`, `create_holiday`, `update_holiday`, `delete_holiday`,
    `create_no_teach_week`, `update_no_teach_week`, `delete_no_teach_week`, `create_week_theme`,
    `update_week_theme`, `delete_week_theme`, `create_deadline`, `update_deadline`, `delete_deadline`.

Must:
  The endpoint is served at `/mcp` through the `mcp` SDK's Streamable HTTP transport with JSON responses.
  Read tools work without any credentials. Each write tool requires an `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header
  whose token equals the `AIKANA_MCP_TOKEN` environment variable, compared constant-time; when the variable is
  unset or empty, every write tool is rejected, so the interface fails closed.
  A rejected write call is reported as a tool error carrying a message, not as an HTTP error, so the MCP session
  stays usable.
  Dates and times on the wire are ISO 8601 (`yyyy-mm-dd` dates, `HH:MM` times); the `d.m.yyyy` display rule in
  /aikana.sdd governs rendered views only, not this machine interface.
  Entity dicts carry the entity's own fields with integer ids; a Semester dict additionally carries its computed
  `start` and `end` bounds, so an agent can plan without re-deriving the period rules.
  Write tools return the created or updated entity dict; delete tools return `{"deleted": id}`.
  Read tools carry the SDK's `readOnlyHint` annotation and delete tools its `destructiveHint` annotation, so
  agents can tell them apart.
  DNS-rebinding protection is disabled on the Streamable HTTP app: the app serves a public Dokku hostname, which
  the SDK's default localhost allowlist would reject with `421`.

Must not:
  ./services.py never imports the `mcp` SDK, so the adaptation layer stays unit-testable without it, per
  ../architecture.sdd.
  ./services.py and ./server.py must not open a database connection or query one directly; all persistence goes
  through the feature packages' services.py, per ../architecture.sdd.
  The token must not be logged or rendered in tool output.

Tasks:
  [x] Implement ./services.py: @McpWriteGuard, @McpService, @McpError and the entity serializers
  [x] Implement ./server.py: @create_mcp_server with the read and write tools, and wire it into ../main.py
  [x] Add the WeekTheme read and write tools for ../week_themes/week_themes.sdd, whose `week_start` goes on the wire
    as the ISO `yyyy-mm-dd` Monday of the themed week
  [x] Add the Deadline read and write tools for ../deadlines/deadlines.sdd, whose `date` goes on the wire as an ISO
    `yyyy-mm-dd` date
